content:
{
  "asset": "P-104 standby pump, AquaDyne HF-300 on the filtered-water line; serial plate painted over and unreadable.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature is 69 C. The applicable HF-300 limits are for housing-surface measurement: normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. Therefore 69 C is within the normal range, 1 C below the normal upper limit, 11 C below alarm and 21 C below trip. It does not trigger SSP-07's priority-1 rule for temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is 3.0 mm/s. The supplied HF-300 manual identifies 'high vibration' as a symptom but gives no numerical velocity limit or severity zones. Consequently, this reading cannot be classified against a documented limit, and it cannot be established whether SSP-07's highest-severity-zone immediate-stop rule applies.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The steadily leaking shaft seal matches the manual's leakage-at-shaft-seal fault symptom, for which the corrective action is mechanical seal replacement and alignment checking. No numerical allowable leakage rate is supplied for comparison with the reported steady leak.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "First inspect for worn or cracked seal faces, the most direct documented explanation for shaft-seal leakage. If P-104 is serial HF3-22000 or above and still contains HF3-450, early failure caused by the revised sleeve tolerance is an additional serial-specific possibility documented by the service bulletin.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is the next hypothesis because it is a documented cause of seal leakage and is also included in the manual's high-vibration causes; verify it by alignment measurement rather than assuming it from the unclassified 3.0 mm/s reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Dry running is another documented seal-leakage cause. The HF-300 has Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry, but the report does not establish that flush was lost or that dry running occurred.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, misalignment and cavitation/NPSH problems remain documented vibration-related possibilities to inspect. None is confirmed by the supplied readings, and bearing replacement is not justified by temperature alone because 69 C is below the 80 C alarm.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Hold point before seal selection or gland-nut tightening: obtain P-104's verified serial number from reliable asset/manufacturer records or another legible manufacturer marking. Record whether it is below HF3-22000 or is HF3-22000 and above. If this cannot be resolved, do not guess the seal part number or gland torque.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump, complete electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves, and drain and vent before line break under a line-break permit. Use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because P-104 is within the chemically dosed filtered-water pump group.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prepare a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly. Its documented mass is 68 kg, exceeding SSP-07's 25 kg lifting-control threshold. Isolate and drain the pump, then remove the back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, and inspect the seal faces and sleeve for damage and scoring. Review seal-flush/run-dry history and the Plan 11 flush arrangement. For a pump确认为 HF3-22000 or above, replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth; do not apply that bulletin threshold as a documented rejection limit to lower serial numbers.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the reported vibration without prematurely calling it 'high': inspect the bearings and impeller, check alignment and check NPSH/cavitation. Replace both bearings as a pair only if inspection establishes wear, noise or high temperature; 69 C alone is within the normal temperature range.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Select exactly one seal after serial verification. Below HF3-22000, use component seal HF3-450 and the manual procedure. At HF3-22000 and above, do not fit HF3-450; use pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, for which no sleeve setting measurement is needed. Continue to inspect the sleeve for scoring. Fit the selected new seal and a new HF3-120 casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble using the manual's Table 5 torques on lightly oiled threads where applicable: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut 160 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm if disturbed. For a verified below-HF3-22000 pump using HF3-450, tighten M10 seal gland nuts to 25 Nm. For HF3-22000 and above using HF3-450B, use the bulletin's 30 Nm gland torque instead of 25 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Perform laser shaft alignment after the seal work and whenever work has moved the motor or bearing housing. Meet the documented tolerances of 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to standby service, restore the Plan 11 flush arrangement as applicable and never run the pump dry. On controlled restart, check the seal repair and repeat housing-temperature and vibration measurements. Apply the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip limits; if vibration is subsequently established to be in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Component mechanical seal — conditional alternative, quantity 1 only if P-104 is verified below serial HF3-22000. Do not fit it on HF3-22000 or above, and do not supply both alternative seals for installation.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal — conditional alternative, quantity 1 only if P-104 is verified as serial HF3-22000 or above. It supersedes HF3-450 in that serial range; select exactly one seal after serial verification.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, quantity 1; fit a new gasket during seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, quantity 1 conditional on inspection. On serial HF3-22000 and above, replacement is required when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth; otherwise retain as a contingency rather than automatically replacing it.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the 68 kg back pull-out assembly: lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment, because the load exceeds 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-104 is between P-101 and P-106 on the chemically dosed filtered-water line using sodium hypochlorite; wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional vibration control: if the current or a subsequent reading is shown to be in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The supplied evidence does not establish that 3.0 mm/s is in that zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: standard labour allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8.0 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard labour allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician. Together with seal replacement, the documented base allowance is 9.5 technician-hours, excluding unquantified additional troubleshooting or repairs.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement only if inspection establishes the documented replacement criteria: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians for replacing the pair. This is not included in the base seal-repair allowance.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection conflict: manual Revision D parts list identifies HF3-450, while Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 and requires HF3-450B on serial HF3-22000 and above. The bulletin explicitly leaves lower serial pumps on HF3-450 and the manual. Decision for P-104: applicability is unresolved because its serial is unreadable; the bulletin's date alone does not make it applicable. Hold seal selection until the serial is verified, then apply the stated serial-range decision.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas the bulletin gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B on pumps from serial HF3-22000. Decision for P-104: use 25 Nm only for a verified lower-serial pump retaining HF3-450; use 30 Nm for a verified in-scope pump using HF3-450B. Do not select either value while the serial remains unresolved.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is P-104's verified serial number, build applicability and currently installed seal type? These are required to decide between HF3-450 and HF3-450B, between 25 and 30 Nm gland torque, and whether the bulletin's sleeve-scoring rule applies. (C05, C11, C13)",
    "What are the manufacturer's numerical HF-300 vibration limits and highest severity zone, and what measurement basis/location applies to the reported 3.0 mm/s? Without them, the vibration severity and any immediate-stop obligation cannot be decided. (C09, C15)",
    "If P-104 is below HF3-22000 and its sleeve is scored, what rejection criterion should be used? The manual requires scoring inspection but gives no numerical limit, while the 0.1 mm criterion is restricted to the bulletin serial range. (C10, C13)",
    "Was there any loss of Plan 11 flush or dry-running event, and what do seal-face, alignment, bearing, impeller and NPSH inspections show? These facts are needed to establish root cause and any scope beyond seal replacement and alignment. (C02, C09)",
    "What additional labour is required for vibration troubleshooting, sleeve replacement or other findings? The supplied labour table only standardsies seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment. (C12)"
  ]
}
